21:["$","section",null,{"className":"section theme-light","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"wrap","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":680},"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"Questions"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"h2","style":{"marginTop":18},"children":"Good to know."}]]}],["$","$L17",null,{"children":["$","$L26",null,{"items":[["Can you integrate Shopify with any ERP?","We've integrated with NetSuite, SAP B1, Sage, Microsoft Dynamics, Brightpearl, Cin7, Linnworks, QuickBooks and custom-built ERPs. If it has an API, we can integrate it."],["What's the difference between a native Shopify app integration and a custom API integration?","Native app integrations are faster to implement and maintained by the app vendor. Custom API integrations give you control over the exact data that flows, how it's transformed, and when — necessary when app-based integrations lack the flexibility your operation requires."],["How do you handle integration failures?","Every integration we build includes error logging, retry logic and alerting. If a sync fails, your team is notified with enough context to understand what happened — and the integration attempts recovery automatically before requiring manual intervention."]]}]}]]}]}]
